    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSU229/postdoctoral-research-associate": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate at The University of Edinburgh Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Postdoctoral Research Associate The University of Edinburgh - School of Engineering - Institute for Imaging, Data and Communications Location: Edinburgh Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 1st September 2026 Closes: 14th September 2026 Job Ref: 14727 Full time: 35 hours per week Fixed term: for 6 months Where curiosity becomes impact With roles from hospitality to research, there’s a career for everyone at the University of Edinburgh. We can offer opportunities for you to develop in your career and make a real difference in the communities around us while contributing to the world at large. We offer careers and roles in just about every area you can think of. Whether you are looking for entry-level, mid-career or roles at the top of your chosen specialism, we can offer you a career where you can flourish and make a real difference in the communities around us while contributing to the world at large. Our people come from a wide range of backgrounds, each bringing their abilities and experiences to our organisation. The University isn’t just any employer. We are part of a local community and a contributor to global thinking, progress and research. In Edinburgh, you are in one of the world’s most attractive cities with active arts and social sectors, while working in a University that has made significant contributions to society, medicine, physics and teaching for over four centuries. Our people have helped create the modern world and are working on more ground-breaking technologies and practices. Join the University of Edinburgh and you’ll be making a difference to everything around you The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We look for the best in the field across all disciplines and provide a working environment where academics can develop their careers and passion for their chosen subject area. We offer the full range of academic roles and have a genuine focus on our students performance and wellbeing. The Opportunity The Research Associate position will contribute to the project ‘Beyond Line-of-Sight Diffuse Optical Wireless Communication (BOLD) within the Institute for Imaging, Data and Communications (IDCOM) at the University of Edinburgh. The role is UE07 and is available on a 6 months fixed term contract. A full list of main responsibilities and the knowledge, skills and experience required for the role can be found in the full job description below. Your skills and attributes for success: A PhD and first degree in Communications Engineering, Electronic Engineering or a closely related subject Experience of electronic systems design including PCB layout/prototyping. Knowledge and experience of Optical Communications Knowledge and experience of experimental optical wireless communications system design and modelling. Knowledge and experience physical layer design for digital communication systems. Experience of carrying out experiments in optical communication systems. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been succ