    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST125/postdoctoral-research-associate-in-landscape-natural-capital-accounting-and-biodiversity-reporting": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting at The University of Edinburgh Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting The University of Edinburgh - CSE - School of GeoSciences - Institute for Geography and the Lived Environment Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 27th August 2026 Closes: 21st September 2026 Job Ref: 14707 Full Time: 35 hours per week Fixed term: 20 th November 2027 Together we can do great things. Be part of something bigger. Here, you can continue to make a difference in everything around you. Take on new challenges, grow your career, be recognised for your contributions, and benefit from our commitment to your wellbeing. Be part of something bigger — where your work has real impact and your development matters. There are so many reasons to take your next step with us. The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We look for the best in the field across all disciplines and provide a working environment where academics can develop their careers and passion for their chosen subject area. We offer the full range of academic roles and have a genuine focus on our student’s performance and wellbeing. The opportunity: Advance urban and landscape-scale natural capital accounting and biodiversity reporting methods through action research in Scotland. We are looking for an interdisciplinary researcher with knowledge and experience in natural capital or ecosystem accounting to work within the Centre for Sustainable Forests and Landscapes on the Horizon Europe funded CircHive project until November 2027 to develop and new natural capital accounting methodologies to support urban and rural natural capital and biodiversity reporting. The post holder will co-develop and test natural capital accounts with the University of Edinburgh Forest and Peatland (FPP) landscape restoration project and the City of Edinburgh Council (CEC) to deliver useful and usable approaches to support decision-making. Your skills and attributes for success: Experience in applying natural capital concepts Experience using a range of data analysis methods Ability to communicate complex information clearly, orally and in writing Experience of working collaboratively in large, diverse teams PhD, or equivalent professional experience relevant to the role Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failur