    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSU209/project-manager-business-analyst": {
      "title": "Project Manager/Business Analyst",
      "description": "Project Manager/Business Analyst at The University of Edinburgh Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Project Manager/Business Analyst The University of Edinburgh - ISG - Applications Directorate - Project Services Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        (pro rata for part time staff) (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 1st September 2026 Closes: 18th September 2026 Job Ref: 14642 Full time: 35 hours per week Open ended (permanent) Vacancies available: 2 Join the University of Edinburgh and you’ll be making a difference to everything around you. Be part of something bigger — where you’ll do meaningful work, grow and progress, be rewarded and recognised, and benefit from our strong commitment to your wellbeing. There are so many reasons to join us. The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We are a large University covering a wide range of activities. In Professional Services, we support the University’s research and teaching, offering many career and role specialisms. The opportunity: We are looking for two enthusiastic and experienced Project Manager/Business Analysts to join Project Services which is part of the Information Services Group (ISG). We are an established specialist team of dynamic and friendly project and programme delivery professionals supporting IT and business change at the University. Working as part of our team, you will get involved with a wide variety of projects, utilising your excellent project management and business analysis skills to deliver successful outcomes for the University. Projects could include improving business efficiency, enhancing student experience, maintaining IT compliance and enabling digital transformation. The post is open-ended, and has a hybrid working pattern, involving working on campus one to two days a week and when necessary for in-person meetings and activities.  Working hours are ideally 35 hours per week, but we will consider flexible working requests. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunate