    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS599/research-associate-in-superconducting-aircraft-propulsion-motors": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors",
      "description": "Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors at The University of Edinburgh Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors The University of Edinburgh - CSE - School of Engineering Location: Edinburgh Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 25th August 2026 Closes: 15th September 2026 Job Ref: 14794 Full Time: 35 hours per week Fixed term: up to 24 months The Opportunity: Develop the future of sustainable aviation Where curiosity becomes impact With roles from hospitality to research, there’s a career for everyone at the University of Edinburgh. We can offer opportunities for you to develop in your career and make a real difference in the communities around us while contributing to the world at large. The University of Edinburgh is a world-leading research-intensive university (QS ranking top 35), committed to excellence, innovation and making a positive contribution to society. As part of our diverse and inclusive community, you will work with colleagues at the SuperMachine Group and the Superconducting Electrical Futures (SEF) Lab in the School of Engineering, who share a passion for addressing global net zero challenges through superconducting technologies The School of Engineering is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors to join a €5m Horizon Europe consortium project led by Dr Hongye Zhang at the University of Edinburgh. This 24-month, full-time role will contribute to the development of superconducting motor windings for fully electric, hydrogen fuel-cell-powered aircraft. You will undertake research involving the multiphysics modelling, design, testing and evaluation of superconducting propulsion motor technologies. You will work closely with Dr Hongye Zhang and EU/UK academic/industrial partners across the project consortium, contributing to project milestones, technical reports, publications and presentations. We are looking for a highly motivated researcher with a PhD, or equivalent experience, in electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, thermal engineering, aerospace engineering, physics or a related discipline. You should have strong analytical and research skills, together with knowledge or experience relevant to electric machines, applied superconductivity, or aerospace technologies. Experience with electro-mechanical-thermal modelling, cryogenic systems, superconducting materials, motor windings or hydrogen-electric propulsion would be advantageous. The role offers an opportunity to contribute to internationally significant research addressing the transition to cleaner aviation. Occasional travel to consortium meetings, conferences or partner facilities may be required. Laboratory work may involve cryogenic liquids, including liquid nitrogen, and will be supported by appropriate training and risk assessments. We encourage applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds and experiences who can contribute to our values of excellence, integrity, inclusion, relevance and ambition. Apply now to join the project team and help develop innovative propulsion technologies for the future of sustainable aviation. A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle, including: A competitive pension scheme Generous annual leave allowance Staff discounts and a wide range of health and wellbeing support Professional development and training opportunities Family-friendly and inclusive policies Employee networks and support for a diverse and welcoming community Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy appl