    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST113/dataloch-developer": {
      "title": "DataLoch Developer",
      "description": "DataLoch Developer at The University of Edinburgh Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results DataLoch Developer The University of Edinburgh - CMVM - School of Population Health Sciences - Usher Institute - Dataloch Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 27th August 2026 Closes: 9th September 2026 Job Ref: 14692 Full Time: 35 hours / week Fixed term: 18-months The opportunity: Where passion meets purpose. Be part of something bigger. Make a meaningful impact. Here, you can continue to make a difference in everything around you. Take on new challenges, grow your career, be recognised for your contributions, and benefit from our commitment to your wellbeing. Be part of something bigger — where your work has real impact and your development matters. There are so many reasons to take your next step with us. The Usher Institute at the University of Edinburgh has a vacancy for an experienced Dataloch Developer to provide programming and software engineering solutions to support DataLoch.   DataLoch is a data service that supports health care research and innovation with secure access to health data. As a Developer within our team you will be responsible for providing programming and software engineering solutions to support our service, contributing to the development and continuous improvement of our systems portfolio and data architecture, working with a varied mix of stakeholders from research, technical and clinical backgrounds. Professional Services The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We are a large University covering a wide range of activities. In Professional Services, we support the University’s research and teaching, offering many career and role specialisms. People have always been at the heart of our work. Our people are at the centre of the University community and everything we do. We value colleagues with drive, determination and a passion for what they do. We are a place where everyone is welcome and offer a range of policies and benefits designed to support you in building the right meaningful flexibility that works for you. A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle: Professional development and subject matter expertise Opportunities to develop new skills and broaden your experience Responsibility and autonomy This post is full-time (35 hours per week); however, we are open to considering part-time or flexible working patterns. We are also open to considering requests for hybrid working (on a non-contractual basis) that combines a mix of remote and regular on-campus working. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation